# CS-340 Client & Server Development: Animal Shelter Dashboard

## Project Overview

The Animal Shelter Dashboard was developed as part of CS-340: Client and Server Development at Southern New Hampshire University. The purpose of this project was to build an interactive dashboard that connected a MongoDB database to a Python application using Dash and Plotly.

The dashboard allows users to search, filter, and visualize animal shelter data while displaying the information in an organized and user-friendly format. This project focused on database connectivity, data retrieval, CRUD operations, data visualization, and dashboard development.

---

## Project Requirements

The project was developed for Grazioso Salvare, a company that needed a way to quickly search and analyze animal shelter records to identify dogs that could be trained for search-and-rescue operations.

The dashboard includes:

- MongoDB database integration
- Interactive data tables
- Search and filtering functionality
- Data visualization
- Geographic mapping
- CRUD operations
- Dashboard widgets
- Dynamic data updates

---

## Software Design and Development

One of the most important design decisions I made was creating a reusable CRUD Python module that separated the database logic from the dashboard itself.

Keeping the database functionality separate from the user interface made the code easier to read, maintain, test, and modify. If database changes are needed in the future, I only need to update the code in one location instead of making changes throughout the entire application.

The biggest advantage of this approach was reusability. The same CRUD module could easily be used in future dashboards, web applications, reporting tools, or APIs.

---

## Problem-Solving Approach

For this assignment, I approached the project as a real-world business problem instead of simply completing a programming assignment.

I first identified Grazioso Salvare's requirements and then divided the project into smaller tasks:

1. Database setup
2. CRUD module development
3. Dashboard integration
4. Data visualization
5. Testing and validation

This approach was different from many previous assignments because I had to think about how users would interact with the data instead of focusing only on writing code.

Moving forward, I plan to continue using this step-by-step development process when creating databases and applications for future clients.

---

## Why This Project Matters

Computer scientists develop systems that transform data into useful information.

In this project, the dashboard helps organize, filter, and display large amounts of data quickly, allowing users to make faster and more informed decisions.

This project brought together many of the concepts I learned throughout the Computer Science program, including:

- Python programming
- MongoDB
- CRUD operations
- Client-server architecture
- Dashboard development
- Data visualization
- Database design
- Software engineering

Because of this, the Animal Shelter Dashboard became the perfect artifact for my CS-499 capstone project and demonstrates my growth in software design, algorithms and data structures, and database development.

